  <h2>About Me 🦛</h2>
  <p>
    Hi, I’m LinHeMa — or you can call me Hippo Lin. I like to try new things
    (except dangerous activities… hippos are brave, but not reckless 🦛). I’m
    from Taiwan, and I believe life is better when it’s interesting and
    peaceful. My friends say I’m lovely, positive, and often end up leading
    things without meaning to. I guess hippos have natural main-character
    energy.
  </p>

  <h2>What I do ?</h2>
  <p>
    I’m a frontend developer who loves turning ideas into clear, intuitive
    interfaces. I first entered the world of tech through a bootcamp — learning
    the basics of computer science opened a new path for me, and I’ve been
    hooked ever since. I work mostly with React and Next.js, and I’m especially
    excited about projects that help people understand things more easily.
    Clean, transparent information is kind of my thing.
  </p>

  <h2>Things I Love 🎮🚲🧶</h2>
  <p>
    When I’m not coding, I’m probably:
    <ul>
      <li>Playing games (and losing track of time)</li>
      <li>Riding my bicycle around</li>
      <li>Crocheting something cute and useless</li>
      <li>
        Enjoying good music or joining events like Chillout Music Festival
        Taipei 2025
      </li>
    </ul>

    I love communities that bring people together — especially those built
    around games and music.
  </p>

  <h2>A Bit About Me ✨</h2>
  <p>
    Three words that describe me: <strong
      >Smart, Thoughtful, Independent.</strong
    >
    I want people to feel welcomed when they read this — like we’re just chatting
    over coffee. And yes, I sprinkle in some humor here and there. Life’s better
    that way.
  </p>

  <h2>My Goals & Vision 🚀</h2>
  <p>
    Right now, I’m working on a congress watch website, aiming to make budget
    transparency more accessible. My dream? To do work I actually care about —
    not just work to fill the hours. I hope my work reflects focus and
    dedication, and I’d love to connect with people who love building things,
    admire Taiyo Matsumoto, or vibe with 礼賛 as much as I do.
  </p>
